Default the channel logo path to VDR's shared logo directory.

Channel logos are skin independent artwork; other skins read them from
<resdir>/logos, and distributions ship them there as a separate package.
skindesigner defaulted to <resdir>/plugins/skindesigner/logos instead, a
directory the plugin never installs, so out of the box the default path
pointed at nothing and every setup had to pass -l/--logopath.

Derive the default from vdr.pc like SKINDESIGNER_SCRIPTDIR does, so it
follows a relocated resdir. -l/--logopath still overrides it, and a skin
that ships its own themes/<theme>/logos still wins (see imagecache.c).

The trailing slash is kept: FileExists(path, name, ext) concatenates the
three without a separator.

README and conf/skindesigner.conf document the new default; the README's
logo section also described a skins/<skin>/logos lookup the code no
longer does.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -21,9 +21,13 @@ LIBDIR = $(call PKGCFG,libdir)
 LOCDIR = $(call PKGCFG,locdir)
 PLGCFG  = $(call PKGCFG,plgcfg)
 VDRCONFDIR = $(call PKGCFG,configdir)
-PLGRESDIR = $(call PKGCFG,resdir)/plugins/$(PLUGIN)
+VDRRESDIR = $(call PKGCFG,resdir)
+PLGRESDIR = $(VDRRESDIR)/plugins/$(PLUGIN)
 TMPDIR ?= /tmp
 SKINDESIGNER_SCRIPTDIR ?= $(LIBDIR)/$(PLUGIN)/scripts
+# Channel logos are skin independent, so they live in VDR's shared resource
+# directory rather than below this plugin's own resource directory.
+SKINDESIGNER_LOGODIR ?= $(VDRRESDIR)/logos
 
 ### The compiler options:
 export CFLAGS   = $(call PKGCFG,cflags)
@@ -47,6 +51,7 @@ SOFILE = libvdr-$(PLUGIN).so
 DEFINES += -DPLUGIN_NAME_I18N='"$(PLUGIN)"' $(CONFIG)
 DEFINES += $(shell xml2-config --cflags)
 DEFINES += -DSCRIPTFOLDER='"$(SKINDESIGNER_SCRIPTDIR)"'
+DEFINES += -DLOGOFOLDER='"$(SKINDESIGNER_LOGODIR)"'
 DEFINES += -D__STL_CONFIG_H
 
 INCLUDES += $(shell pkg-config --cflags freetype2 fontconfig)
--- a/README
+++ b/README
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ The following paths can be set at startup:
     (Default: <ConfigDirectory>/plugins/skindesigner/installerskins/)
 
 -l <LOGOPATH>, --logopath=<LOGOPATH>
-    Path to common logo set for all skins (Default: <ResourceDirectory>/plugins/skindesigner/logos/)
+    Path to common logo set for all skins (Default: <ResourceDirectory>/logos/)
 
 -e path, --epgimages=path
     Path to the epgimages (Default: <CacheDirectory>/epgimages/)
@@ -123,13 +123,13 @@ configured vdrOsd Font is used as default.
 Channel Logos
 -------------
 
-Since each XML skin is responsible for it's used channel logos, skindesigner
-searches for channel logos only in the skin dependend directory
+A skin theme can ship its own channel logos in
 
-<ResourceDirectory>/plugins/skindesigner/skins/<skinname>/logos
+<SKINPATH>/<skinname>/themes/<themename>/logos
 
-Each copy your used logos directly to this directory or set a symbolic link to
-a common channellogo directory.
+If that directory does not exist, skindesigner uses the common logo set in
+<LOGOPATH>, by default VDR's shared, skin independent logo directory
+<ResourceDirectory>/logos, where distributions install channel logo packages.
 
 I recommend to use channel logos from https://github.com/3PO/Senderlogos
 To download them just change in the directory you want to place the logos
